<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hawiye</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hawiye are one of the major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> clan families, living mainly in central and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, including Mogadishu, and in parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and Kenya. They are divided into many clans, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abgaal">Abgaal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habar-gidir">Habar Gidir</a>. Hawiye groups overthrew Ajuran rule in the late 17th century and have dominated the politics of Mogadishu since 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hawiye.jpg" alt="Hawiye" width="320" height="111" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carte Ortelius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hawiye_Kingdom_of_the_North_East_in_1570.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
